Link ccv and NNC as one shared library

Each of the six binaries carried its own copy of the 970 MB .nv_fatbin, all
of the ccv host code, and sqlite. WORKSPACE.linux now pre-declares @sqlite3
with a split BUILD, and pins @s4nnc, @ccv and @build_bazel_rules_cuda to the
teaspan forks, which add a cc_shared_library and a cc_import to
nnc/BUILD.bazel and mark the ccv host sub-libraries alwayslink. Eight
Libraries BUILD files redirect @ccv//lib:ccv to @s4nnc//nnc:C_ccv so the
static payload cannot be linked in again. sqlite lives in the shared library
because Store.swift opens handles that ccv_nnc_tensor_read consumes, and
both must use the same sqlite.
